<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohammed bin Salman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1985">1985</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohammed bin Salman is the crown prince of Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, a son of King Salman, and since 2022 also its prime minister. Appointed crown prince in 2017, he concentrated power in his own hands, launched the Vision 2030 programme to diversify the economy away from oil and relaxed social rules such as the ban on women driving. His rule has also been marked by the war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, a sweeping crackdown on dissent and the killing of the journalist Jamal Khashoggi in 2018.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mohammed-bin-salman.jpg" alt="Mohammed bin Salman" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: وكالة الأنباء السعودية · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B5%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B1%D8%B3%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%A9_%D9%84%D9%84%D8%A3%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%B1_%D9%85%D8%AD%D9%85%D8%AF_%D8%A8%D9%86_%D8%B3%D9%84%D9%85%D8%A7%D9%86_%D8%A8%D9%86_%D8%B9%D8%A8%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D8%B2%D9%8A%D8%B2_%D8%A2%D9%84_%D8%B3%D8%B9%D9%88%D8%AF_(%D9%85%D9%82%D8%B5%D9%88%D8%B5%D8%A9).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
